  },
  {
    "episode_id": 50750,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50750.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Well, recently, I was kind of driving to the state house and thinking. I spent most of my life in the United States, all of my mature life. But second most, I spent actually in Soviet Union. That's where I grew up before Soviet Union fell apart and became Ukraine. So I grew up in a socialistic country. I saw what's happened when socialism runs out of money, and it's only a matter of time. And now I am in the country where I build them socialism. So I said, wow, that is like a full circle, terrible, terrible thought. But you know, experience is all parts of health care and knowing what socialized health care is, it's really a terrifying thought for me. So that's what made me become a politician.",
