    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50750.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think it's interesting for me because not that long ago, Milton Friedman was talking, well, we have all of these surpluses. People will be enjoying freedoms. We'll never get into that. And we'll always have enjoyed this free enterprise that will empower a lot of people. And it really didn't take us very long to get to the government control in so many areas. And I would argue that health scare about 90% directly on indirectly controlled by the government. And we kind of forgot completely that the government is the biggest problem that we have in everything, anything but health care education is in trouble. So someone who grew up in 100% monopoly, controlled by government, and with the point we have two choices. We're going to wake up and say, oh, my gosh, we need to go back to free enterprise. It made our nation's greatest in the world. Or a lot of people saying, you know what? Nothing is working. Market is not working. We have 100% government monopoly and control of prices. And it will control prices, but will be fatal for the quality. And people are going to be very, very shocked what is going to be. So I live through that. So I see what next. is",
