    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "I think people just frustrated and people are frustrated and I think that education should come from people like you and me and some other people that understand and know that free enterprise in policy individuals. All of monopolist and government only powers special interests. It suppresses poor and sick and it creates a lot of millionaires and billionaires and expanse of promise and shifting money to poor that never is going to happen anyway. So it's all just doing the political sales and promises that they cannot fulfill. And ultimately, I think Friedman was talking about that the benefit of monopoly, then there is not more to sell and promise to politicians. So at least this partial government control creates a lot of bad incentives. So it's kind of created even more bad stuff. So I think if we want to be honest and say, you know what, we fail. Our country, we felt our people and it's fatal to equality and say we're going to go and get government control with Russian and everything else because that's the only way how monopoly can. So, you know, if we talk about even Medicare, you know, our senior patients, you know, they got it the best, right? Look at Europe. If you're an old and sicker, you're going to be at the end of the line. Okay, you're going to be, I'm sorry, we have to treat youngest first. So you, You don't have to be sorry, dude, you have to die, okay?",
