  {
    "episode_id": 50750,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50750.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 54,
    "turn_text": "Oh, I'm sure. All you always do. You know, the tyranny of status quo, right? It's pretty bad, but you know, as bad as the tyranny of the government, you know, but I think it's very difficult because until, if you have perverse incentives, it's very difficult and I work with a lot of executives, large companies and until it starts moving your bottom line, until it's that effect and you a lot of executives don't really want to do something about things. It's convenient. It's easier. We don't want to overwork generally if we don't have to. But I think as soon as you put the right incentives, a lot of these companies will start moving. And I think the genius out of the bottle, unless they want to have government monopol, and I don't think any stakeholders want that, honestly, and they're going to lose way more,",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
