    "turn_idx": 58,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's the same vision as anything else when we have a competition and supply and demand, you know, making the determining the price and mean consumer buying the direct service. I go on Amazon, buy a book, I go to places, so you have choices what to buy, what kind of service, what I need, what kind of book I want. What I service want, what kind of app I want on my phone, how much I want to load, how much memory. So you decide as a consumer what I really need because we have all different needs and desires. So you have a place I'll be able to determine what the quality of that book or the quality of that service or goods are. I have to be able to shop. I have to be able to shop. And then I have to be able to look in innovative solution. If I have some disease, if I have some type of cancer that cancer is treated in the Mayo Clinic or in Australia or whatever in India, I have to be able to get that service what fits me the best and I will be able to get that treatment or disease or medication. That is something that I'm as a consumer, will be able to help with some specialists, some advice from other doctors or employers. Or maybe even talk, you know, hey, Google, can you suggest me what you see there, you know?",
